L179: ## 4 Experiments
L180: ### 4.1 Benchmarks and Experimental Setup
L181: Polling-based Object Probing Evaluation (POPE). POPE [cite40†16 ] evaluates object hallucinations in LVLMs via binary queries (e.g., “Is there a chair?”). Unlike caption-based methods, it directly probes object recognition and hallucination. The balanced dataset (27K pairs) contains 50% real/50% absent objects from COCO [cite73†17 ], A-OKVQA [cite74†25 ], and GQA [cite75†10 ]. Three sampling strategies: random, popular (frequent objects), adversarial (challenging cases). Evaluation uses Accuracy and F1.
